
## Big Increase

- the figure / graph show a steep / dramatic rise
- ... surged in ..., jumping from ... to ... in a single year
- a brief spike occurred in ..., when ... hit ...
- **climbing by** 25 percentage points **to reach** ... (25 percentage points is how much it changed)
- soared to ... / soared, reaching a peak of ... in ...
- substantial / considerable / significant increase

## Big Decrease

- a substantial / significant drop
- a sharp / steep / dramatic fall
- plunged / plummeted /  nosedive

## Small Change

- slight / modest / marginal decrease
- edged up / inched up by ... / from ... to ...
- a slight dip (giảm nhẹ), slipping from ... to ...
- fluctuate
- rise and fall

## Stabilize

- remain stable
- stay at this level
- finishing at a comparable level
- plateaued at
- hovered around
- levelled off at ...

## Peak

- reached a peak of / peaked at
- hit a low of / bottom out at
- recovered / rebounded to ...
- year ... marked a turning point for ..., after which the trend reversed

## Comparisons

- overtook / surpassed / outstripped
- was ahead of ... / lagged behind ...
- the largest / smallest share

## Proportion language

- made up / accounted for / constituted
- a majority / minority
- roughly / approximately / just under / just over
- two-thirds / three-quarters

## Time range

- over the period / throughout the timeframe

## Overview

- Overall, it is clear that ...
- A notable feature is that

## Increase again

- increase / surge to its previous peak

## Decrease again

- drop back to ...

## Important Adv

- slightly
- rapidly
- steadily

## Other Adv and Adj

- whopping
- a 3-fold surge

## Synonym for experienced

- showed
- recorded
- saw
- there was

## Period

- ... in this period / surveyed timeframe

## Process

- take on the shape of sth

## Sequential processes

- ... before ...
